Strongswan comes only with Ubnutu distribution.

**Ports should be open in VMs**
==> UDP 500 > 0.0.0.0/0 
==> UDP 4500 ==> 0.0.0.0/0

1) First Install the Packages in the Opeating System.
# sudo apt update
# sudo apt install strongswan strongswan-pki libcharon-extra-plugins -y

2) Create directory for CA Certificates (Self Signed CA) along with its respective configurations and location.
# mkdir -p ~/pki/{cacerts,certs,private}
# chmod 700 ~/pki
# ipsec pki --gen --type rsa --size 4096 --outform pem > ~/pki/private/ca-key.pem
# ipsec pki --self --ca --lifetime 3650 \
--in ~/pki/private/ca-key.pem \
--type rsa \
--dn "CN=VPN CA" \      
--outform pem > ~/pki/cacerts/ca-cert.pem     

==> Create certificates for server <===

# ipsec pki --gen --type rsa --size 4096 --outform pem > ~/pki/private/server-key.pem
# ipsec pki --pub --in ~/pki/private/server-key.pem \
| ipsec pki --issue --lifetime 1825 \
--cacert ~/pki/cacerts/ca-cert.pem \
--cakey ~/pki/private/ca-key.pem \
--dn "CN=<YOUR_EC2_PUBLIC_IP>" \
--san="<YOUR_EC2_PUBLIC_IP>" \
--flag serverAuth --flag ikeIntermediate \
--outform pem > ~/pki/certs/server-cert.pem

=> Copy certificates to IPsec directory
# sudo cp -r ~/pki/* /etc/ipsec.d/

3) Configure StrongSwan in their configuration file. 
# sudo vi /etc/ipsec.conf

===> Paste the syntax below & change the IP Address of the VM <====

config setup
    charondebug="ike 2, knl 2, cfg 2"

conn ikev2-vpn
    auto=add
    compress=no
    type=tunnel
    keyexchange=ikev2
    fragmentation=yes
    forceencaps=yes

    left=%any
    leftid=<YOUR_EC2_PUBLIC_IP>
    leftcert=server-cert.pem
    leftsendcert=always
    leftsubnet=0.0.0.0/0

    right=%any
    rightid=%any
    rightauth=eap-mschapv2
    rightsourceip=10.10.10.0/24 (Local IP Address of the VM)
    rightdns=8.8.8.8,8.8.4.4

    eap_identity=%identity

4) Add credentials in the IPsec directory
# sudo vi /etc/ipsec.secrets
   : RSA "server-key.pem"
   username : EAP "password123"

5) Enable IP Forwarding
# sysctl "net.ipv4.ip_forward=1"
# sysctl --system
# sysctl -a | grep net.ipv4.ip_forward"

6) Flush the existing rules and Allow only VPN traffics
# sudo iptables -F

==> Allow loopback
# sudo iptables -A INPUT -i lo -j ACCEPT

==> Allow established
# sudo iptables -A INPUT -m conntrack --ctstate ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT

==> Allow IPsec
# sudo iptables -A INPUT -p udp --dport 500 -j ACCEPT
# sudo iptables -A INPUT -p udp --dport 4500 -j ACCEPT

==> NAT for VPN clients
# sudo iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -s 10.10.10.0/24 -o eth0 -j MASQUERADE

7) Block all traffic and  except only VPN
==> Default drop
# sudo iptables -P OUTPUT DROP

==> Allow VPN traffic out
# sudo iptables -A OUTPUT -p udp --dport 500 -j ACCEPT
# sudo iptables -A OUTPUT -p udp --dport 4500 -j ACCEPT

==> Allow established
# sudo iptables -A OUTPUT -m conntrack --ctstate ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT

==> Allow DNS ONLY via VPN
# sudo iptables -A OUTPUT -o eth0 -p udp --dport 53 -j ACCEPT

==> Prevent DNS Protection
# sudo vi /etc/strongswan.d/charon.conf
   dns1 = 8.8.8.8
   dns2 = 8.8.4.4

8)  Start VPN service and check status
# sudo systemctl restart strongswan-starter
# sudo systemctl enable strongswan-starter
# sudo ipsec status

9) Client Setup in  Mobile
==> Go for new VPN profile option
   ==> Provie VPN's server IP address
   ==> Choose VPN TYPE IKEv2 EAP (Username & Password)
   ==> Import Certificate from VPN server ==> Server certificate file location ==> ~/pki/cacerts/ca-cert.pem
